1794   DB59             ;**************************************************************************
1795   DB59             ;* Adds a new thread to the VM. The data for this routine is contained 
1796   DB59             ;* directly after the jsr to this routine. A single byte follows the
1797   DB59             ;* jsr and is the timer byte used for the delay until the thread starts.
1798   DB59             ;* The actual address directly after the timer byte is where the thread
1799   DB59             ;* will start running. Example:
1800   DB59             ;*
1801   DB59             ;*  jsr addthread
1802   DB59             ;*    .db 05        ;This is the timer byte
1803   DB59             ;*  ldaa #FF        ;This code is executed as the thread.
