3562   E442             
3563   E442             ;This is unused in the macros. You must call it directly at $F1D5
3564   E442             ;The behavior of this command is probably the most complex. It 
3565   E442             ;starts at the last lamp in the range. If it is already set, then
3566   E442             ;the routine simply exits. If the last lamp is not set, the routine
3567   E442             ;goes down through each lamp in the range. If if finds a lamp on,
3568   E442             ;then it turns off that lamp, then goes back up to the next lamp
3569   E442             ;and turns it on. If no lamps are on in the range, then the first
3570   E442             ;lamp in the range is turned on.
3571   E442             ;The best example of this routine is for the 10-20-30 lamps on 
3572   E442             ;Jungle Lord. It will simply incrment the 10-20-30 lamps sequentially
3573   E442             ;and then stop at 30. If none are on, then it will turn on 10.
3574   E442             lampm_g             
3575   E442 8D 4F                       bsr lampr_end               ;A = Last Lamp Level, B = Last Lamp BitPos
3576   E444 26 3A                       bne abx_ret
