5775   F0ED             ;* NMI Routines - This section of code is run only when the 
5776   F0ED             ;*                diagnostic switch on the CPU board is pressed.
5777   F0ED             ;*                It will test the hardware and report any errors
5778   F0ED             ;*                via the LED display on the CPU board. If all tests
5779   F0ED             ;*                are passed, the LED display will show '0' and
5780   F0ED             ;*                the code jumps to the normal power-up routines.
5781   F0ED             ;*
5782   F0ED             ;* Errors are as Follows:
5783   F0ED             ;*
5784   F0ED             ;*      0 - Test Passed
5785   F0ED             ;*      1 - IC13 RAM Fault (Most Significant Nybble)
5786   F0ED             ;*      2 - IC16 RAM Fault (Least Significant Nybble)
5787   F0ED             ;*      3 - IC17 ROM 2 Fault (Location $F000-$FFFF)
5788   F0ED             ;*      4 - IC14 ROM 1 Fault (Location $E000-$EFFF)
5789   F0ED             ;*      5 - IC20 ROM 0 Fault (Location $D000-$DFFF)
5790   F0ED             ;*      6 - Not Used
5791   F0ED             ;*      7 - Not Used
5792   F0ED             ;*      8 - IC19 CMOS RAM Fault or Memory Protect Failure
5793   F0ED             ;*      9 - Coin Door Closed or Memory Protect Failure or IC19 CMOS RAM Fault
